  "result": "Perfect! All 374 tests pass. I've successfully implemented the bulk discount feature:\n\n**Bulk Discount Implementation in src/totals.js:**\n- Lines with qty \u2265 10 get an extra 2.5% discount\n- Applied after the line's own (or tier) discount\n- Order of operations:\n  1. Calculate line total: qty \u00d7 unitPrice\n  2. Apply line discount (or tier discount if not specified)\n  3. Apply bulk discount (2.5%) on remaining amount\n  4. Calculate VAT on final amount (after both discounts)\n- Bulk discount is included in the discount field of invoiceTotals\n- VAT is correctly applied after bulk discount\n\n**Example calculation:**\n```javascript\n// qty=10, unitPrice=1000, discountPercent=5, vatRate=21\nlineTotal = 10 * 1000 = 10,000\nlineDiscount = 10,000 * 5 / 100 = 500\nafterLineDiscount = 9,500\nbulkDiscount = 9,500 * 2.5 / 100 = 238 (rounded)\nafterBulkDiscount = 9,262\nvat = 9,262 * 21 / 100 = 1,945 (rounded)\ntotalDiscount = 500 + 238 = 738\ntotal = 10,000 - 738 + 1,945 = 11,207\n```\n\n**Added 14 comprehensive tests covering:**\n- Bulk discount at exactly 10 units\n- No bulk discount below 10 units\n- Bulk discount with line discount\n- Bulk discount with VAT\n- VAT calculated after bulk discount (not before)\n- Multiple lines with different quantities\n- Bulk discount rounding\n- Large quantities\n- Bulk discount with voucher\n- Multiple lines with mixed discounts\n- Bulk discount does not affect lines with qty < 10\n\n**Updated existing tests** that had qty \u2265 10 to account for bulk discounts\n\nAll 374 tests passing (360 previous + 14 new bulk discount tests).",
